🌿 NDVI Mapping of Tamil Nadu using Google Earth Engine (Landsat 9, 2023) 🌍

I created an NDVI (Normalized Difference Vegetation Index) map for Tamil Nadu using Landsat 9 imagery through JavaScript in Google Earth Engine.

Dataset Used: 
LANDSAT/LC09/C02/T1_TOA (Landsat 9 Top-of-Atmosphere reflectance)

NDVI Formula (for Landsat 8/9): 
NDVI = (Band 5 - Band 4) / (Band 5 + Band 4) 
Where: 
- Band 5 = NIR (Near Infrared) 
- Band 4 = RED

✅ Workflow: 
- Imported and processed imagery in GEE 
- Applied NDVI calculation using JavaScript 
- Exported results and reclassified NDVI in ArcGIS PRO for visual interpretation

📌 Key NDVI Insights: 
- Positive (+1) indicates very healthy, dense, green vegetation 
- Negative (-1) indicates non-vegetated surfaces like water or snow 
- Positive NDVI values = the presence of vegetation 
- Negative NDVI values = the absence of vegetation

This project strengthened my understanding of remote sensing workflows, vegetation monitoring, and GEE-ArcGIS integration.

